From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:44:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] zink: make a pending clear visible to a sampler texture
 barrier

glTextureBarrier with the sampler bit makes what was rendered visible to the
draws that follow, and a clear is rendering. Zink applied a pending clear
before only a framebuffer barrier; for a sampler barrier it was left for the
next render pass to apply as its load operation, in the same pass as the draw
that samples the cleared attachment. A GPU that keeps an attachment in tile
memory until the pass ends, as Metal's does, hands that draw what was in
memory before the clear: Skia's dst reads of a surface it has just cleared
saw the surface's previous contents.

Apply every pending clear before either kind of texture barrier.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c
index 86fd508be22e6b69cd1070b3154fa1413b9716c2..1cf085015d81247e626341e2f10f30e606c3b7c5 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_context.c
@@ -4792,8 +4792,13 @@ zink_texture_barrier(struct pipe_context *pctx, unsigned flags)
                        VK_ACCESS_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_READ_BIT :
                        VK_ACCESS_SHADER_READ_BIT;
 
-   /* if this is a fb barrier, flush all pending clears */
-   if (ctx->rp_clears_enabled && dst == VK_ACCESS_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_READ_BIT)
+   /* A pending clear is a write to the framebuffer the barrier has to make
+    * visible: to an input attachment for a framebuffer barrier, and to the
+    * texture a draw samples an attachment through for a sampler barrier.
+    * Left for the next render pass to apply as its load operation, a clear
+    * is not in memory when that pass's draws sample the attachment, which a
+    * tile-based GPU keeps in its tile memory until the pass ends. */
+   if (ctx->clears_enabled)
       zink_flush_clears(ctx);
 
    /* this is not an in-renderpass barrier */
